    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1140">

                <pb facs="0818" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/66.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Miller to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-14T20:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1914, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Constitutionalist force under General Pablo Gonzalez occupied Tampico yesterday
                    about noon. Perfect order being preserved. Guaranties assured to all foreigners
                    to return to their business.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Miller</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
